    "Q14"
  ],
  "notes": "Two distinct, parallel failure chains converge on TDAFW inoperability: (1) I/P transducer roll-pin defect causing ALHV0010 erratic/uncontrollable behavior (the officially analyzed cause, cause_code TBD as form fields state 'TBD'), and (2) a separate failed actuator on FV-313 causing pump overspeed trip during troubleshooting. Both contributed to exceeding the 72-hour completion time and the eventual NOED invalidation and shutdown. Cause code left as TBD/provisional per FORM-366 fields, which report 'TBD' despite narrative identifying a specific proximate cause; category thus also provisional. ESW modeled as design-context backup source (not stated operable during this specific event window) so no BACKED_UP_BY edge asserted; motor-driven AFW pumps were confirmed operable per narrative but text doesn't name them as EIIS-coded systems distinct enough to model without redundancy with sys_ba trains - omitted per minimal modeling given ambiguity. Previous LER 2024-001-00 captured as stub per rule 9."
}